                <p> 
                </p><pre>PMWATCH - April 14, 2002 --  Those of you who have been watching CNN the last few days could 
not avoid noticing their wall-to-wall, gavel-to-gavel, coverage of the suicide bombing on Friday 
in Jerusalem.  Indeed, CNN was live for 6 hours NON-STOP about the bombing on Friday alone, and 
ever since has been running images of the panic in the market and the mayhem that ensued. Compare 
this to the spotty coverage of the Israeli massacres of Palestinians, their non-coverage of the 
Jenin atrocities, and maybe you can begin to appreciate the extent to which CNN's coverage of 
this crisis has been journalistically abysmal.


But if you want to really understand what makes CNN tick, I invite you to read the following 
note sent to us by a pmwatcher (see below interface).  It vividly illustrates the extent to which 
CNN is scared stiff of the pro-Israeli pressure groups, and how very hard they are trying to 
compensate for even the half-hearted coverage that they are giving to the Palestinian massacres 
-- coverage that falls way short of communicating the horror on the ground.


Note especially how they go so far as to undermine their own reporter, Rula Amin, in their
attempt to appease criticism from the pro-Israeli voices.


Now, what must also be noted is that NEVER is a note of comparable detail ever sent to 
pmwatchers complaing about pro-Israeli bias.  Their complaints, it seems, deserve only the usual
automatic reply.


Please drop a note to CNN by filling the info below and clicking send.  Address your note to: </pre>
                <div align="center">
                  <pre>Mr. Rick Davis   
</pre>
